00:10:04.080 --> 00:10:05.910
Listen up, Hane.

00:10:05.910 --> 00:10:08.620
There are two types of bike modifications:

00:10:08.620 --> 00:10:12.090
First, there's tuning. Then, there's custom.

00:10:12.090 --> 00:10:13.050
Oh, I see!

00:10:13.050 --> 00:10:15.590
Tuning is making it faster,

00:10:15.590 --> 00:10:18.010
and custom is making it cooler.

00:10:18.010 --> 00:10:19.760
Close.

00:10:19.760 --> 00:10:22.640
Tuning is "making it easier to ride".

00:10:22.640 --> 00:10:25.600
On the other hand, custom is
"making it ride worse".

00:10:25.600 --> 00:10:27.310
Making it ride worse?

00:10:27.690 --> 00:10:30.600
But you know, people who
ride bikes are a mystery.

00:10:31.110 --> 00:10:33.190
Despite bikers having other bike friends,

00:10:33.190 --> 00:10:36.940
we still want to have a
identity different from others.

00:10:36.940 --> 00:10:41.200
Like, "This bike rides horribly and I'm the
only one who can even ride it."

00:10:41.200 --> 00:10:42.660
Huh...

00:10:42.660 --> 00:10:46.200
So, what about people who put
anime stickers on their bikes?

00:10:46.200 --> 00:10:47.910
Is that tuning or custom?

00:10:47.910 --> 00:10:48.710
Huh?

00:10:48.710 --> 00:10:52.840
Well it makes it harder to ride
for other people so,

00:10:52.840 --> 00:10:54.170
I guess it's custom?

00:10:54.170 --> 00:10:57.920
Full of yourself again, Shaggy?

00:10:58.590 --> 00:11:01.640
Rin-chan, you came too!

00:11:01.640 --> 00:11:05.890
That's right, you modded your
bike somewhere, right?

00:11:05.890 --> 00:11:07.430
Come look and see.

00:11:10.100 --> 00:11:11.350
Hot plasma!

00:11:11.600 --> 00:11:13.310
A G-Gun Spark!

00:11:14.730 --> 00:11:19.070
Hane, there's another type of bike modification.

00:11:19.070 --> 00:11:20.240
The occult.

00:11:20.240 --> 00:11:22.820
You mean, like ghosts and stuff?

00:11:23.660 --> 00:11:28.200
Parts sold based on doubtful
claims of performance gains.

00:11:28.200 --> 00:11:30.750
These people put them on
their bikes and feel good about it.

00:11:30.750 --> 00:11:34.880
Say Rin, aren't you curious about
how much power you've gained?

00:11:34.880 --> 00:11:37.050
Want to have it tested at my shop?

00:11:37.050 --> 00:11:40.760
What, don't tell me you're one of
those people who care about the specs?

00:11:40.760 --> 00:11:44.180
There are tons of things
you can't put a number on!

00:11:44.760 --> 00:11:46.720
Ah, I get it, I get it!

00:11:46.720 --> 00:11:49.350
It's the sound or the vibration, right?

00:11:49.350 --> 00:11:51.940
I'd prefer that it <i>looks</i> normal, you know?

00:11:51.940 --> 00:11:54.400
This way, I can give it a boost
without changing the look.

00:11:54.400 --> 00:11:57.360
It feels different the moment you install it.

00:11:57.360 --> 00:12:01.860
How could a bike be better if
you didn't even change the parts?

00:12:02.820 --> 00:12:05.160
That's too good to be true!

00:12:08.660 --> 00:12:10.500
I get it.

00:12:10.500 --> 00:12:13.040
I've been there before.

00:12:13.040 --> 00:12:14.630
Onsa-chan...

00:12:14.630 --> 00:12:17.290
Well, that said,

00:12:17.290 --> 00:12:20.420
if there <i>is</i> an exception, it would be...

00:12:20.760 --> 00:12:23.090
Oil additives!

00:12:23.880 --> 00:12:26.050
This one's the real deal.

00:12:26.050 --> 00:12:27.810
Add this when you do an oil change,

00:12:27.810 --> 00:12:30.680
and gear shifts feel totally different!

00:12:30.680 --> 00:12:32.730
The gear changes sound so smooth.

00:12:32.730 --> 00:12:36.400
It gives it a huge kick. It sounds so
beautiful when you shift into first.

00:12:36.400 --> 00:12:37.610
It makes you want to shift for no reason.

00:12:37.610 --> 00:12:39.780
That's too good to be true!

00:12:44.240 --> 00:12:46.160
What do you think, Yume?

00:12:46.160 --> 00:12:47.200
Huh?

00:12:47.200 --> 00:12:51.080
What are the best kinds of
parts to make a bike better?

00:12:51.080 --> 00:12:55.120
I don't know much about motorcycles,

00:12:55.120 --> 00:12:57.040
but I don't think it's so easy

00:12:57.040 --> 00:12:59.750
to change the performance that much.

00:12:59.750 --> 00:13:03.050
But people do notice a difference.

00:13:03.050 --> 00:13:07.590
That's probably all in the person's head.

00:13:07.590 --> 00:13:08.720
Their head?

00:13:09.010 --> 00:13:12.730
People love their bikes, right?

00:13:12.730 --> 00:13:17.480
They want to spend time, effort,
and money on their bikes.

00:13:17.480 --> 00:13:23.110
So it's probably fun just putting
all kinds of parts on them.

00:13:24.030 --> 00:13:27.660
Parts to make motorcycles more fun, huh?

00:13:27.660 --> 00:13:29.030
That's it!

00:13:29.030 --> 00:13:33.250
It's kinda weird how oil additives only
have an affect when you change your oil!

00:13:33.250 --> 00:13:36.830
Compared to that, hot plasma makes
your bike better the moment you put it on!

00:13:36.830 --> 00:13:39.290
That's still way too good to be true!

00:13:39.290 --> 00:13:41.250
Rin-chan! Onsa-chan!

00:13:41.250 --> 00:13:44.260
Look, I found some super cool parts!

00:13:44.260 --> 00:13:47.890
I think you'll both love it!

00:13:48.590 --> 00:13:50.100
It's as easy as sticking it on!

00:13:50.100 --> 00:13:53.310
I actually already put it on your bikes!

00:13:53.680 --> 00:13:54.930
Look!

00:14:01.480 --> 00:14:03.860
Ultra Happy Meter!

00:14:05.780 --> 00:14:07.700
Let me explain this product.

00:14:07.700 --> 00:14:12.660
Simply attach it to the meter,
and it shows double the speed!

00:14:12.660 --> 00:14:15.330
It feels different the moment you install it.

00:14:15.950 --> 00:14:17.040
No way.

00:14:17.040 --> 00:14:18.170
Nope.

00:14:18.170 --> 00:14:19.250
Huh?

00:14:23.670 --> 00:14:25.050
What're you doing?

00:14:25.050 --> 00:14:28.380
I thought it might give me ideas
for the cultural festival race.

00:14:28.380 --> 00:14:31.850
But I don't recognize some of the tools in it.

00:14:32.390 --> 00:14:33.470
Let's see.

00:14:33.470 --> 00:14:38.020
Like this panel that reduces your engine
temperature when you go over it.

00:14:38.020 --> 00:14:40.730
That's only in the game!

00:14:40.730 --> 00:14:43.150
Such a useful panel doesn't exist in reality.

00:14:43.150 --> 00:14:46.240
What? It's all made-up?

00:14:46.820 --> 00:14:51.990
But a race would be so
much more fun with these boards...

00:14:51.990 --> 00:14:54.080
But maybe with Minowa Group,

00:14:54.080 --> 00:14:56.540
Minowa Science's technology...

00:14:56.540 --> 00:14:58.250
I said it's impossible.

00:14:59.080 --> 00:15:00.420
Where's Hane?

00:15:00.420 --> 00:15:05.840
She left early to work on bike
modifications with Raimu-senpai.

00:15:05.840 --> 00:15:06.880
Modifications?

00:15:06.880 --> 00:15:09.720
Aren't you getting ready, too, Onsa-chan?

00:15:10.840 --> 00:15:15.260
I was thinking maybe I'd decorate it
with strobe colors using full wraps.

00:15:15.560 --> 00:15:17.180
Don't you want to win?

00:15:17.180 --> 00:15:19.690
I'm going to do my best, of course,

00:15:19.690 --> 00:15:21.980
but there's only so much
I can do with a Serow.

00:15:21.980 --> 00:15:24.310
There'll be a cash prize, though.

00:15:24.310 --> 00:15:26.320
A cash prize? Are you paying?

00:15:26.320 --> 00:15:28.650
No, it's from our profits.

00:15:28.650 --> 00:15:29.490
Huh?

00:15:29.490 --> 00:15:33.740
The cultural festival race is
going to be a betting race.

00:15:33.740 --> 00:15:34.030
Betting?
The cultural festival race is
going to be a betting race.

00:15:34.030 --> 00:15:34.700
Betting?

00:15:34.700 --> 00:15:36.620
The audience is going to bet?

00:15:36.620 --> 00:15:37.740
Yes.

00:15:37.740 --> 00:15:40.540
That way, even people who have

00:15:40.540 --> 00:15:43.290
no interest in bikes can join in the fun.

00:15:43.290 --> 00:15:46.300
We'll have people cheering for certain riders.

00:15:46.300 --> 00:15:49.260
That's true, but...

00:15:50.630 --> 00:15:50.800
Gold

00:15:50.800 --> 00:15:52.510
Is that what you meant by "gold"?
Gold

00:15:52.510 --> 00:15:54.800
Is that what you meant by "gold"?

00:15:55.640 --> 00:15:58.520
B-But I don't think the school will allow that...

00:15:58.520 --> 00:15:59.560
That's not true.

00:15:59.560 --> 00:16:02.770
The principal gave her approval.

00:16:02.770 --> 00:16:07.070
But she did name a strange condition...

00:16:07.070 --> 00:16:08.730
All right.

00:16:08.730 --> 00:16:13.030
If Raimu-se— I mean, a student
named Kawasaki Raimu joins,

00:16:13.030 --> 00:16:15.740
and if win tickets will be available,

00:16:15.740 --> 00:16:18.120
I'll make an exception and allow

00:16:18.120 --> 00:16:20.660
a race in the cultural festival.

00:16:21.290 --> 00:16:24.330
That's a really suspicious condition...

00:16:24.330 --> 00:16:28.300
But wouldn't your sidecar
or Raimu-senpai's Ninja

00:16:28.300 --> 00:16:30.170
have a huge advantage in a race?

00:16:30.170 --> 00:16:31.720
Not to worry.

00:16:31.720 --> 00:16:35.300
Hayakawa and I will not
be entering the race.

00:16:35.300 --> 00:16:37.800
We'll be emcees instead.

00:16:37.800 --> 00:16:42.350
And we've thought of fair handicaps
for Raimu-senpai, as well.

00:16:42.890 --> 00:16:47.770
These kinds of races are
more fun when they're close.

00:16:47.770 --> 00:16:50.610
It'll be restricted to the
four domestic manufacturers.

00:16:50.610 --> 00:16:51.940
Four bikes, four riders.

00:16:51.940 --> 00:16:55.530
I need you to be well-prepared, too.

00:16:59.410 --> 00:17:01.830
If Raimu-senpai's going to be helping,

00:17:01.830 --> 00:17:04.500
Hane must be doing some serious tuning.

00:17:04.500 --> 00:17:07.960
I thought I could beat
Hane, even on my Serow,

00:17:08.290 --> 00:17:10.090
but this could get tough.

00:17:10.090 --> 00:17:10.380
Nicoichi Motors
but this could get tough.

00:17:10.380 --> 00:17:11.550
Nicoichi Motors

00:17:11.550 --> 00:17:13.050
In which case...
Nicoichi Motors

00:17:13.050 --> 00:17:15.340
So, you want to win?

00:17:15.340 --> 00:17:17.680
I'm in it to win now.

00:17:17.680 --> 00:17:21.310
I won't use it on public roads, so a large bike
or one with expired insurance would work.

00:17:21.310 --> 00:17:23.810
In that case, I have a winning machine.

00:17:23.810 --> 00:17:24.850
Really?

00:17:24.850 --> 00:17:27.060
You mean the YZF-R1?

00:17:27.600 --> 00:17:31.020
We don't have a properly working R1 here.

00:17:31.610 --> 00:17:34.610
It's true. All our bikes are scrap.

00:17:34.610 --> 00:17:38.660
I won't have time for repairs
before the festival.

00:17:43.290 --> 00:17:44.330
Isn't that...

00:17:44.910 --> 00:17:47.330
The unusual center-raised muffler...

00:17:47.330 --> 00:17:47.500
Back
Front
Exhaust
Vapor
The unusual center-raised muffler...

00:17:47.500 --> 00:17:49.330
A unique layout with the carburetor

00:17:49.330 --> 00:17:50.000
in front of the engine,
a front-vapor, back-exhaust...

00:17:50.000 --> 00:17:53.210
Exhaust
Front
Back
Back
Front
Exhaust
in front of the engine,
a front-vapor, back-exhaust...

00:17:53.210 --> 00:17:53.420
in front of the engine,
a front-vapor, back-exhaust...

00:17:53.420 --> 00:17:57.090
This is the biggest failure in
Yamaha motorcycle history,

00:17:57.090 --> 00:18:00.600
the second-generation TZR250 3MA!

00:18:00.600 --> 00:18:02.180
Also known as the Sanma!

00:18:02.180 --> 00:18:04.020
Bingo.

00:18:04.020 --> 00:18:08.060
I used to ride this bike a long time ago.

00:18:08.060 --> 00:18:11.980
I ran in races, too, but I could never win.

00:18:11.980 --> 00:18:14.530
Still, this was cutting-edge at the time.

00:18:14.530 --> 00:18:17.150
I believed it was the best machine available

00:18:17.150 --> 00:18:19.910
and tried to get it to go faster.

00:18:20.280 --> 00:18:24.120
I'll get laughed at if I ride this
old two-stroke engine bike.

00:18:24.120 --> 00:18:26.410
Hey, Dad, could I at least—

00:18:26.410 --> 00:18:28.750
Come on, Onsa, get on.

00:18:28.750 --> 00:18:30.920
I got it ready for public roads.

00:18:34.880 --> 00:18:38.220
Okay, I'll take it around the block.

00:18:38.220 --> 00:18:39.380
Sure.

00:18:40.550 --> 00:18:42.510
See you.

00:18:43.600 --> 00:18:45.430
I'm back.

00:18:45.890 --> 00:18:47.810
Welcome back.

00:18:47.810 --> 00:18:51.310
Dad, I hate to say it, but this is no good.

00:18:51.610 --> 00:18:54.610
The engine sounds horrible,
it pumps out tons of smoke,

00:18:54.610 --> 00:18:57.990
it's stalled five times since I left,
and worst of all, it's slow.

00:18:57.990 --> 00:18:59.820
Of course it is.

00:18:59.820 --> 00:19:04.120
You can't ride it the same way you ride an
inline-four Serow and expect it to work well.

00:19:04.120 --> 00:19:05.080
But...

00:19:05.410 --> 00:19:08.620
Racer replicas with two-stroke engines

00:19:08.620 --> 00:19:11.330
need a little more revving.

00:19:11.710 --> 00:19:14.290
Take it for another lap.

00:19:17.710 --> 00:19:21.840
No wonder two-stroke engines went extinct.

00:19:21.840 --> 00:19:24.260
The noise, the smoke, the smell...

00:19:24.550 --> 00:19:29.180
Two-stroke engines aren't built
to go on modern roads, are they?

00:19:29.560 --> 00:19:32.770
I guess the one upside is that they're
lighter because they have fewer parts.

00:19:32.770 --> 00:19:35.020
What else is good about it?

00:19:51.330 --> 00:19:54.210
She finally got it up to 7,000 revs.

00:19:56.960 --> 00:20:00.720
Mad acceleration as soon
as it's in the power band...

00:20:01.010 --> 00:20:04.640
Now I know the actual reason
two-stroke engines went extinct.

00:20:04.640 --> 00:20:08.640
Because it's a very naughty bike!

00:20:09.520 --> 00:20:13.350
I can beat the Super Four and Katana on this!

00:20:19.650 --> 00:20:23.740
Of course the Sanma was terrible for racing.

00:20:23.740 --> 00:20:27.080
It was crazy for the manufacturers to stick with

00:20:27.080 --> 00:20:30.910
the 3MA after the next-gen machine,
the 3XV, came out.

00:20:31.710 --> 00:20:34.210
But as time passed,

00:20:34.210 --> 00:20:37.130
bike parts and tuning both evolved.

00:20:37.880 --> 00:20:40.210
It took twenty years after it was discontinued.

00:20:40.210 --> 00:20:42.300
It was a long time coming,

00:20:42.300 --> 00:20:46.930
but we can finally get the Sanma to go fast.

00:20:51.220 --> 00:20:53.980
I went pretty far.

00:20:53.980 --> 00:20:57.270
I could have ridden longer if
my butt hadn't gotten so hot.

00:20:57.270 --> 00:20:58.690
Onee-chan!

00:20:58.690 --> 00:21:00.610
Welcome home!

00:21:01.360 --> 00:21:03.200
Yama-bou, Ha-bou.

00:21:03.200 --> 00:21:05.820
Take a look. It's your sister's racing bike!

00:21:05.820 --> 00:21:07.280
Isn't it awesome?

00:21:08.910 --> 00:21:09.870
Hey...

00:21:09.870 --> 00:21:12.790
Can we attach drills to it to
make it even more awesome?

00:21:12.790 --> 00:21:13.750
Drills!

00:21:13.750 --> 00:21:17.580
Sure, but don't make it too awesome.

00:21:17.580 --> 00:21:19.090
Okay!

00:21:21.300 --> 00:21:22.840
Drills, huh?

00:21:22.840 --> 00:21:25.130
They're still such little kids.

00:21:25.130 --> 00:21:27.090
Done!

00:21:28.390 --> 00:21:30.390
Ta-da!

00:21:32.810 --> 00:21:36.770
Um, listen, can we not put drills on the seat?

00:21:36.770 --> 00:21:39.440
No way! This is what makes it awesome!

00:21:39.440 --> 00:21:41.570
Get on, get on!

00:21:44.070 --> 00:21:47.320
Onee-chan, what are you doing?

00:21:47.320 --> 00:21:51.080
We're modding my Super Four
for the cultural festival.

00:21:51.080 --> 00:21:54.120
With so many turn signals and mirrors?

00:21:54.120 --> 00:21:56.500
Racing is dangerous.

00:21:56.500 --> 00:22:00.000
That's why safety has to come first!

00:22:09.090 --> 00:22:10.800
buon!  buon!  buon!  buon!  buoon!

